      "narrationText": "Apple Cider Vinegar!\n-\nRanked!\n-\nSimple one.\n-\n0.9 grams of carbs. And that is basically the whole nutrition story.\n-\n0 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 0 out of 9, with 0% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nNo real vitamin story here.\n-\nNo real mineral story here.\n-\nPros first: a useful low-calorie flavor tool. As a swap for heavy sauces or dressings, it has some real value. Can still earn points as a better swap. The category should reward harm reduction when it is real. Use case can matter more than macros. This category is really about function and trade-offs.\n-\nCons next: health claims are usually exaggerated. The item tends to be oversold way beyond what it deserves. Rarely deserves to be treated as a foundation food. Most of these are situational, not core nutrition plays. Easy to overrate or misuse. This category attracts strong marketing and habits.\n-\nBig strengths are a useful low-calorie flavor tool and can still earn points as a better swap, but the biggest weaknesses are health claims are usually exaggerated and rarely deserves to be treated as a foundation food.\n-\nB tier.\n"
