      "narrationText": "Beef Tallow!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n100 grams of fat. Cholesterol is 109 milligrams, supporting a better fat profile.\n-\n0 grams of carbs. No defensible carb submacros to call out. Not relevant here.\n-\n0 grams of protein. No defensible protein submacros to call out. Also not relevant here.\n-\nVitamin K is 8% daily value, adding useful vitamin support. Vitamin A is only 0% daily value, a weak mark for oils and fats.\n-\nIron is 0% daily value, useful for oxygen transport. Magnesium is only 0% daily value, a weak mark for oils and fats.\n-\nPros first: helps meals actually work. A fat that people can use well matters more than a theoretical one. Small amounts can change a whole meal. That leverage matters when the fat quality is good. Highly useful in cooking. Practical culinary value matters here.\n-\nCons next: extremely calorie dense by default. That is the unavoidable category burden. Small serving errors matter quickly. A little extra oil or fat can move the calorie math fast. Easy to overpour without noticing. Practical portion creep is real.\n-\nBig strengths are helps meals actually work and small amounts can change a whole meal, but the biggest weaknesses are extremely calorie dense by default and small serving errors matter quickly.\n-\nD tier.\n"
