      "narrationText": "Broccoli!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n0.4 grams of fat. Omega 3 is 40 milligrams, supporting a more useful fat profile. Polyunsaturated fat is 0 grams, a weak mark for vegetables.\n-\n6.6 grams of carbs. Glycemic index is 10 GI, supporting better carb quality. Starch is 0 grams, a small miss for vegetables.\n-\n2.8 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 2 out of 9, with 35% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nVitamin K is 85% daily value, adding useful vitamin support. Vitamin A is 12% daily value, a weak mark for vegetables.\n-\nPotassium is 9% daily value, useful for fluid balance. Iron is only 4% daily value, a weak mark for vegetables.\n-\nThe upsides first: very strong micronutrient payoff. Likely to challenge spinach for elite vegetable status. Good fibre support. Solid maintenance-and-repair fit. Strong cruciferous reputation. Viewed as a flagship healthy vegetable.\n-\nThe drawbacks next: taste can be polarising. Not universally loved. Prep matters a lot. Overcooking hurts it badly. Can be rough on digestion for some. A practical downside.\n-\nBig strengths are omega 3 and carb quality, but the biggest weaknesses are taste can be polarising and prep matters a lot.\n-\nA tier.\n"
