      "narrationText": "Canola Oil!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n100 grams of fat. Saturated fat is 7.4 grams, supporting a better fat profile.\n-\n0 grams of carbs. No defensible carb submacros to call out. Not relevant here.\n-\n0 grams of protein. No defensible protein submacros to call out. Also not relevant here.\n-\nVitamin K is 71% daily value, adding useful vitamin support. Vitamin A is only 0% daily value, a weak mark for oils and fats.\n-\nIron is 0% daily value, useful for oxygen transport. Magnesium is only 0% daily value, a weak mark for oils and fats.\n-\nThe upsides first: can help meals feel more complete and usable. Fats sometimes improve the whole plate, not just their own stats. Highly useful in cooking. Practical culinary value matters here. Small amounts can change a whole meal. That leverage matters when the fat quality is good.\n-\nCons next: easy to overpour without noticing. Practical portion creep is real. Extremely calorie dense by default. That is the unavoidable category burden. Small serving errors matter quickly. A little extra oil or fat can move the calorie math fast.\n-\nBig strengths are fat quality and vitamin K, but the biggest weaknesses are easy to overpour without noticing and extremely calorie dense by default.\n-\nA tier.\n"
