          {
            "kind": "section",
            "sectionKey": "vitamins",
            "text": "Vitamin E is 22% daily value, adding useful vitamin support."
          },
          {
            "kind": "section",
            "sectionKey": "minerals",
            "text": "Magnesium is 91% daily value, adding useful mineral support. Zinc is 32% daily value, a weak mark for seeds."
          },
          {
            "kind": "section",
            "sectionKey": "pros",
            "text": "Positives first: usually brings decent fat support. That is one of the category strengths. Often brings dense micronutrient support. That is part of what makes the category interesting. Easy to sprinkle into meals. That practical versatility matters."
          },
          {
            "kind": "section",
            "sectionKey": "cons",
            "text": "The drawbacks next: spice-like serving sizes limit real payoff. The numbers look huge, but people do not eat 100 grams of cumin seeds. Texture or prep can be a barrier. Not everyone uses seeds consistently. Paper scores can overstate realistic serving sizes. People often eat far less than 100 grams."
          },
          {
            "kind": "closing_summary",
            "text": "Big strengths are protein and vitamin E, but the biggest weaknesses are spice-like serving sizes limit real payoff and texture or prep can be a barrier."
          },
          {
            "kind": "final_reveal",
            "text": "C tier."
          }
