      "narrationText": "Dark Chocolate 85%!\n-\nRanked!\n-\nSimple one.\n-\n46 grams of carbs. And that is basically the whole nutrition story.\n-\n8 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 3 out of 9, with 50% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nNo real vitamin story here.\n-\nNo real mineral story here.\n-\nPros first: meaningfully better than typical candy. The misc ranking should reward better swaps, not just raw perfection. Clear real-world role. If a misc item helps or harms behavior, that matters a lot. Can still earn points as a better swap. The category should reward harm reduction when it is real.\n-\nCons next: still very much a dense treat. It cannot escape being a treat food just because it is darker. Rarely deserves to be treated as a foundation food. Most of these are situational, not core nutrition plays. Better replacements often exist. That practical comparison matters.\n-\nBig strengths are iron and meaningfully better than typical candy, but the biggest weaknesses are still very much a dense treat and rarely deserves to be treated as a foundation food.\n-\nA tier.\n"
