      "narrationText": "Electrolyte Tablet Drink!\n-\nRanked!\n-\nSimple one.\n-\n1 gram of carbs. And that is basically the whole nutrition story.\n-\n0 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 0 out of 9, with 0% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nNo real vitamin story here.\n-\nNo real mineral story here.\n-\nPros first: can be a clean hydration tool. Especially compared with sugary sports drinks, this is a better functional option. Context tells the real story. That is the whole point of misc. Use case can matter more than macros. This category is really about function and trade-offs.\n-\nThe drawbacks next: most people do not need it constantly. Useful tool, but not an everyday necessity. Not a whole-food nutrition star. Most misc items are weak on raw nutrient profile. Rarely deserves to be treated as a foundation food. Most of these are situational, not core nutrition plays.\n-\nBig strengths are a clean hydration tool and context tells the real story, but the biggest weaknesses are most people do not need it constantly and not a whole-food nutrition star.\n-\nA tier.\n"
