      "narrationText": "Flax Seeds!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n42.2 grams of fat. Omega 3 is 22813 milligrams, supporting a more useful fat profile.\n-\n28.9 grams of carbs. Fibre is 27.3 grams, helping with digestion and steadier meals. Starch is 1.6 grams, a small miss for seeds.\n-\n18.3 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 6 out of 9, with 55% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nVitamin E is 2% daily value, adding useful vitamin support.\n-\nMagnesium is 95% daily value, adding useful mineral support. Calcium is 19% daily value, a weak mark for seeds.\n-\nPros first: absurd omega-3 density. This should threaten the top of the seeds category. Extreme fibre density. Another elite seed trait. Strong mineral support. Very hard to dismiss nutritionally.\n-\nCons next: best used ground/processed appropriately. Whole-seed use can reduce payoff. Not universally loved. Practical downside. Can be rough for some. Very high fibre is not free for everyone.\n-\nBig strengths are omega 3 and protein, but the biggest weaknesses are best used ground/processed appropriately and not universally loved.\n-\nS tier.\n"
