      "narrationText": "Grapes!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n0.2 grams of fat. Saturated fat is 0.1 grams, supporting a better fat profile. Polyunsaturated fat is 0 grams, a weak mark for fruits.\n-\n18.1 grams of carbs. Sugar is 15.5 grams, supporting better carb quality. Starch is 0 grams, a meaningful miss for fruits.\n-\n0.7 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 1 out of 9, with 30% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nVitamin C is 6% daily value, useful for collagen formation and antioxidant support. Vitamin A is only 2% daily value, a weak mark for fruits.\n-\nPotassium is 5% daily value, useful for fluid balance. Magnesium is only 1% daily value, a weak mark for fruits.\n-\nPros first: polyphenol case is stronger than the sugar suggests. Tests whether fruit context can rescue sugary but still respected fruits. Very easy to eat. Highly practical fruit. Hydrating and easy. Practical plus.\n-\nThe drawbacks next: sugar load is high for fruit. A real stress test for the fruit ruleset. Fibre moderation is weak. Much weaker than elite fruits. Easy to overeat quickly. Can rack up sugar fast.\n-\nBig strengths are omega 3 and polyphenol case is stronger than the sugar suggests, but the biggest weaknesses are sugar load is high for fruit and fibre moderation is weak.\n-\nD tier.\n"
