      "narrationText": "Palm Oil!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n100 grams of fat. Cholesterol is 0 milligrams, supporting a better fat profile.\n-\n0 grams of carbs. No defensible carb submacros to call out. Not relevant here.\n-\n0 grams of protein. No defensible protein submacros to call out. Also not relevant here.\n-\nVitamin E is 19% daily value, adding useful vitamin support. Vitamin A is only 0% daily value, a weak mark for oils and fats.\n-\nIron is 0% daily value, useful for oxygen transport. Magnesium is only 0% daily value, a weak mark for oils and fats.\n-\nPros first: helps meals actually work. A fat that people can use well matters more than a theoretical one. Efficient energy source. That can be a strength in the right context. Small amounts can change a whole meal. That leverage matters when the fat quality is good.\n-\nDownsides next: calorie density is brutally high. Tiny serving errors matter here. Extremely calorie dense by default. That is the unavoidable category burden. Small serving errors matter quickly. A little extra oil or fat can move the calorie math fast.\n-\nBig strengths are helps meals actually work and efficient energy source, but the biggest weaknesses are calorie density is brutally high and extremely calorie dense by default.\n-\nC tier.\n"
