      "narrationText": "Poppy Seeds!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n41.6 grams of fat. Polyunsaturated fat is 28.5 grams, helping with cell structure and healthy signalling.\n-\n28.1 grams of carbs. Fibre is 19.5 grams, helping with digestion and steadier meals. Starch is 2 grams, a small miss for seeds.\n-\n17.9 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 6 out of 9, with 74% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nVitamin E is 10% daily value, adding useful vitamin support.\n-\nMagnesium is 198% daily value, adding useful mineral support. Iron is 54% daily value, a weak mark for seeds.\n-\nThe upsides first: usually brings decent fat support. That is one of the category strengths. Easy to sprinkle into meals. That practical versatility matters. Easy to sprinkle into meals for a real upgrade. Seeds often shine as support foods.\n-\nCons next: paper scores can overstate realistic serving sizes. People often eat far less than 100 grams. Texture or prep can be a barrier. Not everyone uses seeds consistently. Real serving sizes are often small. Some strong paper numbers are hard to cash out in practice.\n-\nBig strengths are protein and fibre, but the biggest weaknesses are paper scores can overstate realistic serving sizes and texture or prep can be a barrier.\n-\nB tier.\n"
