      "narrationText": "Processed Honey!\n-\nRanked!\n-\nSimple one.\n-\n82.4 grams of carbs. And that is basically the whole nutrition story.\n-\n0.3 grams of protein. No defensible protein submacros to call out. No real protein story here.\n-\nNo real vitamin story here.\n-\nNo real mineral story here.\n-\nPositives first: pleasant natural sweetener identity. People value it as a recognisable sweetener rather than as structural nutrition. Easy to use in drinks and foods. Simple practical upside. Familiar and common. That keeps it relevant to score at all.\n-\nCons next: mostly concentrated sugar. That is the main reason this lands weakly in a context-driven category. Heat processing weakens the case further. Processed honey loses some of the argument raw honey might have made. Overall payoff is weak for misc. The upside does not outweigh the sugar concentration strongly enough.\n-\nBig strengths are pleasant natural sweetener identity and easy to use in drinks and foods, but the biggest weaknesses are mostly concentrated sugar and heat processing weakens the case further.\n-\nD tier.\n"
