      "narrationText": "Watermelon Seeds (Unsalted)!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n47.4 grams of fat. Polyunsaturated fat is 14.6 grams, helping with cell structure and healthy signalling.\n-\n15.3 grams of carbs. Sugar is 0.4 grams, supporting better carb quality. Starch is 2 grams, a small miss for seeds.\n-\n28.3 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 7 out of 9, with 78% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nVitamin E is 2% daily value, adding useful vitamin support.\n-\nMagnesium is 129% daily value, adding useful mineral support. Calcium is only 5% daily value, a weak mark for seeds.\n-\nPros first: easy to sprinkle into meals for a real upgrade. Seeds often shine as support foods. Tiny food with serious nutrient density. Seeds often overperform for their size. Often brings dense micronutrient support. That is part of what makes the category interesting.\n-\nCons next: texture or prep can be a barrier. Not everyone uses seeds consistently. Real serving sizes are often small. Some strong paper numbers are hard to cash out in practice. Calorie density still stacks up fast. Tiny foods can still overshoot fast.\n-\nBig strengths are protein and magnesium, but the biggest weaknesses are texture or prep can be a barrier and real serving sizes are often small.\n-\nC tier.\n"
