        "narrationText": "Avocado Oil!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n100 grams of fat. Saturated fat is 11.6 grams, supporting a better fat profile.\n-\n0 grams of carbs. No defensible carb submacros to call out. Not relevant here.\n-\n0 grams of protein. No defensible protein submacros to call out. Also not relevant here.\n-\nVitamin K is 14% daily value, adding useful vitamin support. Vitamin A is only 0% daily value, a weak mark for oils and fats.\n-\nIron is 0% daily value, useful for oxygen transport. Magnesium is only 0% daily value, a weak mark for oils and fats.\n-\nThe upsides first: small amounts can change a whole meal. That leverage matters when the fat quality is good. Highly useful in cooking. Practical culinary value matters here. Helps meals actually work. A fat that people can use well matters more than a theoretical one.\n-\nDownsides next: calorie density is brutally high. Tiny serving errors matter here. Easy to overpour without noticing. Practical portion creep is real. Easy to overuse without noticing. Liquid calories are slippery in the kitchen.\n-\nBig strengths are fat quality and small amounts can change a whole meal, but the biggest weaknesses are calorie density is brutally high and easy to overpour without noticing.\n-\nB tier.\n"
