        "narrationText": "Cashews!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n43.9 grams of fat. Saturated fat is 7.8 grams, supporting a better fat profile. Omega 3 is 70 milligrams, and for nuts, fat quality has to justify the calories.\n-\n30.2 grams of carbs. Starch is 23.5 grams, supporting better carb quality. Fibre is 3.3 grams, a small miss for nuts.\n-\n18.2 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 6 out of 9, with 74% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nVitamin E is 4% daily value, adding useful vitamin support.\n-\nMagnesium is 73% daily value, adding useful mineral support. Iron is 37% daily value, a weak mark for nuts.\n-\nThe upsides first: holds up as a better snack default than most packaged options. That real-world swap value counts. Fat and texture help satiety. They can hold up better than many snack foods. Portable, practical snack food. Nuts score real points in life because they are easy to use.\n-\nDownsides next: portion control can get slippery fast. Dense foods punish casual handful math. Cost or allergy issues can limit use. Practical downsides still count. Good versions can get expensive. That affects how realistic frequent use is.\n-\nBig strengths are protein and magnesium, but the biggest weaknesses are portion control can get slippery fast and cost or allergy issues can limit use.\n-\nA tier.\n"
