        "narrationText": "Cassava!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n0.3 grams of fat. Omega 3 is 20 milligrams, supporting a more useful fat profile. Polyunsaturated fat is 0.1 grams, a weak mark for tubers.\n-\n38.1 grams of carbs. Starch is 34 grams, supporting better carb quality. Glycemic index is 94 GI, a meaningful miss for tubers.\n-\n1.4 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 1 out of 9, with 30% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nVitamin C is 34% daily value, useful for collagen formation and antioxidant support. Vitamin A is only 0% daily value, a weak mark for tubers.\n-\nPotassium is 6% daily value, useful for fluid balance. Iron is only 2% daily value, a weak mark for tubers.\n-\nThe upsides first: major staple-energy role globally. Tests whether practical staple legitimacy can rescue rough carb behaviour. Very versatile staple. Broad use cases. Does bring some vitamin C. Not empty on micros.\n-\nCons next: glycemic behaviour is brutal. A direct stress test for the tuber ruleset. Fibre payoff is weak. Poor for a stronger tuber. Preparation matters for safety. Not a trivial downside.\n-\nBig strengths are omega 3 and protein, but the biggest weaknesses are glycemic behaviour is brutal and fibre payoff is weak.\n-\nC tier.\n"
