        "narrationText": "Coffee!\n-\nRanked!\n-\nSimple one.\n-\n0 grams of carbs. And that is basically the whole nutrition story.\n-\n0.3 grams of protein. No defensible protein submacros to call out. No real protein story here.\n-\nNo real vitamin story here.\n-\nNo real mineral story here.\n-\nPositives first: strong misc-category fit. Coffee is still fundamentally judged by effects and use-case rather than nutrient composition. Strong alertness effect. This is the main real-world reason coffee matters in this category. Usually near-zero calories plain. Very clean base use-case when not loaded with extras.\n-\nDownsides next: caffeine tradeoffs are real. Sleep disruption, jitters, and overuse risk stop this from being a clean automatic S. Habit dependence can creep in. A stronger practical downside than green tea usually carries. People often ruin it with sugary add-ins. The practical version consumed is not always the clean black-coffee version.\n-\nBig strengths are strong misc-category fit and strong alertness effect, but the biggest weaknesses are caffeine tradeoffs are real and habit dependence can creep in.\n-\nB tier.\n"
