        "narrationText": "Cottage Cheese!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n4.3 grams of fat. Saturated fat is 1.7 grams, supporting a better fat profile. Polyunsaturated fat is 0.1 grams, a weak mark for dairy.\n-\n3.4 grams of carbs. Sugar is 2.7 grams, supporting better carb quality. Starch is 0 grams, a small miss for dairy.\n-\n11.1 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 8 out of 9, with 92% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nVitamin B12 is 13% daily value, useful for nerve and blood-cell support. Vitamin A is only 4% daily value, a weak mark for dairy.\n-\nCalcium is 8% daily value, adding useful mineral support. Magnesium is only 2% daily value, a weak mark for dairy.\n-\nThe upsides first: lean high-protein dairy. Tests whether greek yogurt is the only clean dairy S. Very filling. Strong practical upside. Fairly simple food. Strong dairy identity without dessert drift.\n-\nThe drawbacks next: can be fairly salty. Practical downside. Texture is divisive. Not universally liked. Not suitable for everyone. Tolerance varies.\n-\nBig strengths are omega 3 and protein, but the biggest weaknesses are fairly salty and texture is divisive.\n-\nS tier.\n"
