        "narrationText": "Whole-Wheat Couscous!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n0.6 grams of fat. Saturated fat is 0.1 grams, supporting a better fat profile. Omega 3 is 20 milligrams, a weak mark for grains.\n-\n77.4 grams of carbs. Sugar is 0 grams, supporting better carb quality. Fibre is 5 grams, a meaningful miss for grains.\n-\n12.8 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 4 out of 9, with 58% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nVitamin E is 0% daily value, adding useful vitamin support.\n-\nMagnesium is 11% daily value, adding useful mineral support. Potassium is only 5% daily value, a weak mark for grains.\n-\nPros first: usually affordable and scalable. Practicality matters for staple foods. Useful staple energy source. That matters because grains are often judged by how practical they are in real diets. Works as a meal anchor. A lot of value comes from being easy to build around.\n-\nCons next: easy to overshoot portions. Staple carbs can pile up fast without much friction. Needs strong pairings to feel complete. The grain rarely finishes the nutrition job alone. Carb load is still the main burden. That is the category risk no grain fully escapes.\n-\nBig strengths are protein and usually affordable and scalable, but the biggest weaknesses are easy to overshoot portions and needs strong pairings to feel complete.\n-\nC tier.\n"
