        "narrationText": "Kombucha (Unsweetened)!\n-\nRanked!\n-\nSimple one.\n-\n3 grams of carbs. And that is basically the whole nutrition story.\n-\n0 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 0 out of 9, with 0% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nNo real vitamin story here.\n-\nNo real mineral story here.\n-\nPositives first: can replace much worse drinks. That substitution value matters more than raw micronutrients here. Clear real-world role. If a misc item helps or harms behavior, that matters a lot. Can still earn points as a better swap. The category should reward harm reduction when it is real.\n-\nDownsides next: easy to overpay for the health halo. The benefits are usually less magical than the branding suggests. Not a whole-food nutrition star. Most misc items are weak on raw nutrient profile. Easy to oversell beyond what the numbers support. Misc items often attract exaggerated narratives.\n-\nBig strengths are can replace much worse drinks and clear real-world role, but the biggest weaknesses are easy to overpay for the health halo and not a whole-food nutrition star.\n-\nA tier.\n"
