          "narrationBlocks": [
            {
              "kind": "hook_food",
              "text": "Mozzarella!"
            },
            {
              "kind": "hook_ranked",
              "text": "Ranked!"
            },
            {
              "kind": "section",
              "sectionKey": "fats",
              "text": "17 grams of fat. Cholesterol is 54 milligrams, supporting a better fat profile. Saturated fat is 11 grams, a weak mark for dairy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "section",
              "sectionKey": "carbs",
              "text": "3.1 grams of carbs. Sugar is 1 gram, supporting better carb quality. Starch is 0 grams, a small miss for dairy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "section",
              "sectionKey": "proteins",
              "text": "28 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 8 out of 9, with 92% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance. Collagen is only 0 grams, a weak mark for dairy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "section",
              "sectionKey": "vitamins",
              "text": "Vitamin B12 is 28% daily value, useful for nerve and blood-cell support. Vitamin A is 12% daily value, a weak mark for dairy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "section",
              "sectionKey": "minerals",
              "text": "Calcium is 51% daily value, adding useful mineral support. Magnesium is only 5% daily value, a weak mark for dairy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "section",
              "sectionKey": "pros",
              "text": "Positives first: can be a very convenient protein vehicle. Convenience is one of dairy’s strongest practical advantages. Easy to fit into familiar meals. That lowers friction for regular use. Clear calcium identity. That is a core category strength."
            },
            {
              "kind": "section",
              "sectionKey": "cons",
              "text": "Downsides next: fat quality varies wildly across dairy. Some dairy is clean, some really is not. Not everyone tolerates dairy well. That is a real use-case limitation. Tolerance varies a lot person to person. A category strength is less useful if the food does not agree with you."
            },
            {
              "kind": "closing_summary",
              "text": "Big strengths are protein and carb quality, but the biggest weaknesses are fat quality varies wildly across dairy and not everyone tolerates dairy well."
            },
            {
              "kind": "final_reveal",
              "text": "A tier."
            }
          ],
