        "narrationText": "Plain Yogurt!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n3.3 grams of fat. Cholesterol is 13 milligrams, supporting a better fat profile. Omega 3 is 20 milligrams, a weak mark for dairy.\n-\n4.7 grams of carbs. Sugar is 4.7 grams, supporting better carb quality. Starch is 0 grams, a small miss for dairy.\n-\n3.5 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 7 out of 9, with 90% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance. Collagen is only 0 grams, a weak mark for dairy.\n-\nVitamin B12 is 18% daily value, useful for nerve and blood-cell support. Vitamin A is only 2% daily value, a weak mark for dairy.\n-\nCalcium is 12% daily value, adding useful mineral support. Magnesium is only 3% daily value, a weak mark for dairy.\n-\nPros first: easy to fit into familiar meals. That lowers friction for regular use. Easy protein delivery for normal diets. Dairy gets real credit for convenience. Clear calcium identity. That is a core category strength.\n-\nDownsides next: tolerance varies a lot person to person. A category strength is less useful if the food does not agree with you. Processing changes the category a lot. The label alone does not tell the whole story. Not everyone tolerates dairy well. That is a real use-case limitation.\n-\nBig strengths are omega 3 and protein, but the biggest weaknesses are tolerance varies a lot person to person and processing changes the category a lot.\n-\nC tier.\n"
