        "narrationText": "Pumpkin Seeds!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n49 grams of fat. Polyunsaturated fat is 20.7 grams, helping with cell structure and healthy signalling.\n-\n10.7 grams of carbs. Fibre is 6 grams, helping with digestion and steadier meals. Starch is 1.5 grams, a small miss for seeds.\n-\n30.2 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 7 out of 9, with 78% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nVitamin E is 15% daily value, adding useful vitamin support.\n-\nMagnesium is 141% daily value, adding useful mineral support. Calcium is only 5% daily value, a weak mark for seeds.\n-\nThe upsides first: often brings dense micronutrient support. That is part of what makes the category interesting. Usually brings decent fat support. That is one of the category strengths. Easy to sprinkle into meals. That practical versatility matters.\n-\nCons next: calories concentrate quickly. Even useful support foods can get dense fast. Calorie density still stacks up fast. Tiny foods can still overshoot fast. Texture or prep can be a barrier. Not everyone uses seeds consistently.\n-\nBig strengths are protein and magnesium, but the biggest weaknesses are calories concentrate quickly and calorie density still stacks up fast.\n-\nB tier.\n"
