        "narrationText": "Sunflower Seeds!\n-\nRanked!\n-\n51.5 grams of fat. Polyunsaturated fat is 23.1 grams, helping with cell structure and healthy signalling.\n-\n20 grams of carbs. Fibre is 8.6 grams, helping with digestion and steadier meals. Starch is 5 grams, a small miss for seeds.\n-\n20.8 grams of protein. Essential amino acids score is 6 out of 9, with 76% bioavailability, making the protein useful for repair and maintenance.\n-\nVitamin E is 175% daily value, adding useful vitamin support.\n-\nMagnesium is 104% daily value, adding useful mineral support. Calcium is 8% daily value, a weak mark for seeds.\n-\nPros first: usually brings decent fat support. That is one of the category strengths. Easy to sprinkle into meals. That practical versatility matters. Tiny food with serious nutrient density. Seeds often overperform for their size.\n-\nDownsides next: texture or prep can be a barrier. Not everyone uses seeds consistently. Calorie density still stacks up fast. Tiny foods can still overshoot fast. Real serving sizes are often small. Some strong paper numbers are hard to cash out in practice.\n-\nBig strengths are protein and vitamin E, but the biggest weaknesses are texture or prep can be a barrier and calorie density still stacks up fast.\n-\nS tier.\n"
