              "title": "Cons",
              "narration": "Cons next: refining strips out much of the fibre and micronutrient value. That is the central reason white rice scores worse than intact whole grains. It is mostly starch with limited standalone nutrition. The protein, fibre, and micronutrient payload are all modest for the calories. Carb quality changes a lot with rice type and preparation. That makes the exact glycemic story hard to lock honestly from a single dry-rice record.",
